TO7/70 Experiment
=================

0000-3FFF	4 x 16K cartridge (Fuix overlays)
4000-5FFF	Video RAM (fixed)
6000-60FF	Monitor RAM
6100-9FFF	Fixed (bank 1)
A000-DFFF	6 x 16K plus optionally another 4 with an odder encoding
E000-E7AF	ROM
E7B0-E7FF	I/O
E800-FFFF	ROMs


Memory Map:

0000-3FFF	Banked ROM 	0-3	Cartridge ROM (in our case it'll need to be a Fuzix cart)
4000-5FFF	2 x 8K bank	Bank 0 in 2 8K chunks (some modes need 1 some 2 some use 2 banks)
				(Video is always in this bank)
6000-9FFF	Banked RAM
6000-60FF	Reserved for firmware
6100-9FFF	Fixed RAM	1
A000-DFFF	Banked RAM	6 banks for the rest of the 128K) another 4 differently encoded
				  if the RAM expansion is present
E000-E7AF	ROM (disc usually)
E7B0-E7FF	Devices
E800-FFFF	ROM		0-1

Bootstrap we would fill kernel A000-DFFF from the cartridge then run from
cartridge mostly.

Memory mapping:

Cartridge	:	0000-3FFF	Kernel (4 overlays)
4000-5FFF	:	Video
(unlike the TO9 I don't think we can steal any of this back)
6000-9FFF	:	Monitor + User (might need some kernel common)
A000-DFFF	:	Kernel data/user space/user copy banks
E000-FFFF	:	All owned by the firmware

We have to run in a kind of banked thunked model as we have so little
common space we can use wihtout stealing from our 32K user space.

